1. Linux kernel user-space API constants

   src/compat/*.h define numeric constants and structure layouts taken from
   the Linux kernel's user-space API headers:

     include/uapi/linux/landlock.h
     include/uapi/linux/seccomp.h
     include/uapi/linux/audit.h
     include/uapi/linux/capability.h
     include/uapi/linux/prctl.h
     include/uapi/asm-generic/unistd.h

   Copyright (C) the Linux kernel contributors, including
   Mickael Salaun (Landlock) and Will Drewry and Kees Cook (seccomp).

   These headers are licensed GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note. The
   Linux-syscall-note states that user-space programs which use the kernel
   through normal system calls, including by using these headers, are not
   derived works of the kernel. landlock uses them only in that way and copies
   no kernel code beyond the constants and structure definitions.

